[00:06.04] Night, her sable dome scattered with diamonds
[00:11.01] Fused my dust from a light year
[00:17.67] Squeezed me to her breast, sowed me with carbon
[00:22.32] Strung my warp across time
[00:29.22] Gave me each horse, sunrise and graveyard
[00:33.94] Told me only I was hers
[00:38.66] Bid me face the east closed me in questions
[00:43.07] Built the sky for my dawn
[00:48.24] 
[01:28.89] "Worship", cried the clown, "I'm a TV"
[01:33.38] Making bandsmen go clockwork
[01:39.43] See the slinky seal cirkus policeman
[01:44.12] Bareback ladies have fish"
[01:50.38] Strongmen by his feet, plate-spinning statesman
[01:55.09] Accrobatically juggling
[01:59.30] Bids his tamers go quiet the tumblers
[02:03.90] Lest the mirror stop turning
[02:07.84] 
[03:25.36] Elephants forgot, force-fed on stale chalk
[03:29.83] Ate the floors of their cages
[03:36.36] Strongmen lost their hair, paybox collapsed
[03:40.52] While lions sharpened their teeth
[03:47.55] Gloves raced round the ring, stallions stampeded
[03:52.15] Pandemonium seesaw
[03:56.08] I ran for the door, ringmaster shouted
[04:00.87] "All the fun of the circus"
[04:05.27] 